{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"p0300","type":"group","x":-50,"y":700,"width":1500,"height":680,"color":"2","label":"Results — What (5-6 min)"},
		{"id":"p0200","type":"group","x":-50,"y":-20,"width":1500,"height":660,"color":"3","label":"Methodology — How (6-7 min)"},
		{"id":"p0100","type":"group","x":-50,"y":-700,"width":1000,"height":620,"color":"1","label":"Opening — Problem & Context (3 min)"},
		{"id":"p0400","type":"group","x":-50,"y":1480,"width":1000,"height":500,"color":"6","label":"Conclusion — So What (3 min)"},
		{"id":"p0001","type":"text","text":"# 🎓 FYP Oral Presentation Structure\n15-20 min talk + 5-10 min Q&A\nBSc Financial Mathematics — Yirong Yu (2253235)","x":100,"y":-900,"width":700,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"p0010","type":"text","text":"## Slide 1: Title (30s)\n\nName, ID, programme\n\"Multiplicative Directional-Robust Loss\nfor Cross-Sectional Stock-Return Prediction\"\n\nCore idea in one sentence:","x":0,"y":-660,"width":280,"height":460,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"p0011","type":"text","text":"## Slide 2: Background & RQs (2min)\n\n**Mismatch**: MSE trains calibration\nbut portfolio trades **ranking**\n\nHeavy tails: σ=19.5%, max +2400%\n\n→ 3 Research Questions","x":320,"y":-660,"width":280,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"p0012","type":"text","text":"## Slide 3: Literature (1min)\n\n3 streams:\n1. ML for stock prediction\n2. Robust regression\n3. Directional losses (MADL/GMADL)\n\n**Gap**: no controlled comparison","x":640,"y":-660,"width":280,"height":380,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"p0020","type":"text","text":"## Slide 4: Pipeline (1min)\n\nData → MLP → Loss → Portfolio → Eval\n\n**Single-factor design**: only loss varies\n\nNot architecture search","x":0,"y":20,"width":280,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"p0021","type":"text","text":"## Slide 5: Contributions (1min)\n\n1. Hybrid loss design (A & M families)\n2. M2-robust γ variance penalty\n3. Staged evidence protocol\n4. Bounded recommendation","x":320,"y":20,"width":280,"height":290,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"p0022","type":"text","text":"## Slide 6: Architecture & Data (1.5min)\n\nMLP[64,32,16], 15 inputs (X1)\nTrain: 1990-94 | Test: 1995-96 (24mo)\n\nPhase 1/2: ReLU+drop0.2\nPhase 3: tanh+drop0.0\n→ Within-phase = strongest evidence","x":640,"y":20,"width":330,"height":290,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"p0023","type":"text","text":"## ⭐ Slide 7: Loss Functions (2-3min)\n\n**Key slide — spend time here**\n\nRegression: MSE, MedSE\nDirectional: MADL, GMADL, IMADL\n\nAdditive: L = λ_dir·D + λ_hub·H\n**Multiplicative**: L = (1+λ_dir·D)·H\n\nD = [1-σ(a·y·ŷ)] · |y|^b / E[|y|^b]\n→ sign-sensitive, magnitude-aware, batch-normed\n\n**M2-robust**: L_M2 + γ·Var(ŷ)","x":1010,"y":20,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"p0030","type":"text","text":"## Slide 10: Data & Features (1min)\n\nCRSP-style, 449K obs, 10,987 stocks\nX1: CR & CO at 5 horizons + 5 base\nTarget: r(t+1), no leakage\n\n**No winsorisation** — tails are the point","x":0,"y":740,"width":280,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0031","type":"text","text":"## Slide 11: Phase 1 Baselines (1min)\n\nMSE: Sharpe -0.46 ❌\nMedSE: Sharpe +0.09 (barely)\nGMADL: R² = -7×10⁹ but Sharpe +0.20\n→ **R² and Sharpe decouple**\n\nhybrid_mul_m1: **Sharpe 0.44** 🏆","x":320,"y":740,"width":300,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0032","type":"text","text":"## Slide 12: A/M Sweep (1min)\n\nAdditive peak: A3 Sharpe 0.57\nMultiplicative peak: M1 Sharpe 0.44\n\nM-family R² more controlled\n→ carried to γ refinement\n\nA5 and M3 collapse: form matters","x":660,"y":740,"width":280,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0033","type":"text","text":"## ⭐ Slide 13: γ Refinement (1.5min)\n\n**Core robustness evidence**\n\nγ=03: unstable (CV 1.06)\nγ=05: Sharpe 0.71, CV 0.21\n**γ=07: Sharpe 0.92, CV 0.18** ✅\nγ=10: Sharpe 1.00, CV 0.56 (3× worse)\nγ=15: degrades\n\nNon-monotone: stability peak at 0.7\n→ Best joint Sharpe-stability criterion","x":980,"y":740,"width":380,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0034","type":"text","text":"## Slide 14: α/β/λ Sweeps (1min)\n\nα=06: Sharpe 0.69, CV 0.24, CumRet +30%\n→ Corroborates hybrid-mul direction\n\nβ family: CV 4~140 ❌\nadaptive-λ: underperforms ❌\n\n→ Productive region = hybrid-mul + robust","x":0,"y":1000,"width":340,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0035","type":"text","text":"## ⭐ Slide 15: Normalisation Probe (1min)\n\nTests: are winners just scale artefacts?\n\nγ=07: 0.9156→0.9112 ✅ **stable**\nγ=10: 1.0043→0.4072 ❌ collapses\nα=06: 0.6895→-0.0161 ❌ collapses\n\nNormalisation ≠ universal fix\nOnly γ=07 survives","x":380,"y":1000,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0036","type":"text","text":"## Slide 16: Cumulative Paths (30s)\n\nMSE → downward\nγ=10 → high but wide seed envelope\n**γ=07 → consistent upward across 3 seeds**\n\nVisual proof of stability","x":800,"y":1000,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"p0040","type":"text","text":"## Slide 17: Answering RQs (1min)\n\n**RQ1**: Loss matters — R² and Sharpe\ndecouple (ranks ≠ calibration)\n\n**RQ2**: m2_robust_γ07 best joint\nSharpe 0.92, CV 0.18, CumRet +28%\n\n**RQ3**: Only γ=07 survives normalisation","x":0,"y":1520,"width":300,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"p0041","type":"text","text":"## Slide 18: Recommendation (1.5min)\n\n**Primary**: γ=07 (Sharpe 0.92, CV 0.18)\nHigh-return: γ=10 (Sharpe 1.00, CV 0.56)\nFallback: α=06 (Sharpe 0.69, CV 0.24)\n\n**Limitations**:\n1 window, 3 seeds, 1 feature set\nGross-of-cost, no rolling\n\n**Future**: rolling, ≥10 seeds, costs","x":350,"y":1520,"width":350,"height":250,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"p0042","type":"text","text":"## Slide 19: Close (30s)\n\nLoss function = first-class\ndesign variable for\nportfolio-oriented prediction\n\nγ=07 gives best\nSharpe-stability trade-off\n\nThank you → Q&A","x":750,"y":1520,"width":200,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"p0050","type":"text","text":"## 🎯 Q&A Preparation (Top 10)\n\n| # | Question | Key Answer |\n|---|----------|------------|\n| 1 | Why not optimise Sharpe directly? | Portfolio has non-differentiable ops (ranking, capping). Losses are differentiable proxies. |\n| 2 | Why is R² so negative? | R² = calibration metric. Directional losses preserve ranks, not scale. Portfolio trades ranks. |\n| 3 | Why γ=07 not γ=10? | γ=10 CV is 3× worse; normalisation drops it from 1.00→0.41. γ=07 survives both tests. |\n| 4 | Phase 3 arch difference? | Weakens cross-phase claims. Final rec relies on within-Phase-3 evidence only. |\n| 5 | Why only 3 seeds? | Reveals large CV differences. Need ≥10 for tight CI. CV is order-of-magnitude indicator. |\n| 6 | Why no rolling window? | Static window = clean internal validity. Rolling = future work (regime robustness). |\n| 7 | Why no winsorisation? | Heavy tails = the problem. Clipping them defeats the purpose of robust loss design. |\n| 8 | Transaction costs? | Gross-of-cost. Different losses → different turnover → could change ranking. Future work. |\n| 9 | Why not recommend A3? | Only seed-42 evidence. γ=07 has multi-seed + normalisation probe support. |\n| 10 | Main practical contribution? | Controlled way to treat loss function as portfolio-design variable, with multi-seed stability. |","x":0,"y":2080,"width":950,"height":350,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"p0051","type":"text","text":"## ⏱️ If Time Is Short\n\n**Keep full**: Slides 7 (loss), 10 (data), 13 (γ), 15 (probe), 18 (recommendation)\n**Compress**: Slide 3→3 streams only | Slide 5→1 sentence | Slide 14→\"α=06 corroborates, β/λ don't work\"","x":0,"y":2480,"width":950,"height":120,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"p0060","type":"text","text":"## ⏱️ Timing Guide\n\n| Section | Slides | Time |\n|---------|--------|------|\n| Opening | 1-3 | 3 min |\n| Methodology | 4-9 | 6-7 min |\n| Results | 10-16 | 5-6 min |\n| Conclusion | 17-19 | 3 min |\n| **Total** | **19** | **17-19 min** |\n\n**Q&A**: 5-10 min","x":1050,"y":1520,"width":300,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"p0024","type":"text","text":"## Slide 8: Portfolio & Metrics (1min)\n\nTop/bottom 10% → z-score → 5% cap\nLong-short return each month\n\n**Sharpe** = √12 × mean/std (annualised)\n**CV** = σ_sharpe / |μ_sharpe|\nR² = diagnostic only, not primary metric","x":-100,"y":370,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"p0025","type":"text","text":"## Slide 9: Experimental Phases (30s)\n\nPhase 1: 7 baselines, seed 42\nPhase 2: 9 hybrid variants, seed 42\nPhase 3a: γ × 3 seeds\nPhase 3b: α/β/λ sweeps\nPhase 4: Normalisation probe\n\nAll share same 24-month window","x":540,"y":345,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"3"}
	],
